1
00:00:02,400 --> 00:00:06,351
Prince Ferrix loved the Princess
Crystal, whose face rang like a bell.

2
00:00:06,391 --> 00:00:09,013
When she walked past,
plain iron threw sparks.

3
00:00:10,013 --> 00:00:13,972
THE KING: Give it up, my son. She has
sworn to marry no one but a paleface.

4
00:00:14,572 --> 00:00:16,121
FERRIX: A paleface? What is that?

5
00:00:16,921 --> 00:00:19,713
THE KING: A creature
of slush and splashes.

6
00:00:19,753 --> 00:00:23,006
They began as mold in the
sea, and ate each other,

7
00:00:23,046 --> 00:00:27,484
and stood up on scaffolds of chalk,
and at last they built machines.

8
00:00:27,524 --> 00:00:30,092
Our first father set us free from them.

9
00:00:31,092 --> 00:00:35,223
She tests every suitor. Every one
who is caught lying, she beheads.

10
00:00:36,823 --> 00:00:38,620
FERRIX: Then I will be a paleface.

11
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:49,297
The vizier Polyphase
went into his laboratory

12
00:00:49,337 --> 00:00:51,862
and brewed things that
were gluey and dripping.

13
00:00:53,862 --> 00:00:55,578
POLYPHASE: Shall I go on, Prince?

14
00:00:56,178 --> 00:00:57,305
FERRIX: Do what you must.

15
00:00:58,505 --> 00:01:03,392
Grease and old crud over the steel. Over
that, a paste of chalk and powdered rubies.

16
00:01:03,432 --> 00:01:05,543
On top of the head, a clump of rust.

17
00:01:06,743 --> 00:01:07,860
POLYPHASE: Behold.

18
00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:12,778
FERRIX: Get this abomination off
me! She will hate me on sight!

19
00:01:13,578 --> 00:01:18,325
POLYPHASE: No, Prince. Her madness is that
ugliness is beautiful, and beauty ugly.

20
00:01:19,925 --> 00:01:24,910
Now the inside. Under your cloak, cinnabar.
In your chest, a bellows of dungeon air.

21
00:01:24,950 --> 00:01:27,103
By your eyes, little tubes of water.

22
00:01:27,903 --> 00:01:31,275
When she asks what it is, you
answer. Blood. Breath. Tears.

23
00:01:33,875 --> 00:01:36,133
Polyphase dressed as a portly merchant,

24
00:01:36,173 --> 00:01:39,609
with the books on paleface
customs stuffed inside his robe.

25
00:01:39,649 --> 00:01:42,830
He locked the prince in a
cage and cried him for sale.

26
00:01:43,430 --> 00:01:46,403
POLYPHASE: A young paleface,
from far away! A real one!

27
00:01:47,603 --> 00:01:51,510
PRINCESS CRYSTAL: A hoax. But no one
knows palefaces as I do. Bring him to me.

28
00:01:54,310 --> 00:01:58,160
You worked hard, old man, plastering
this scarecrow with mud and chalk.

29
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:00,830
When I expose it, you
will both lose your heads.

30
00:02:04,230 --> 00:02:05,342
What is that?

31
00:02:06,342 --> 00:02:07,029
FERRIX: Blood!

32
00:02:11,629 --> 00:02:12,741
PRINCESS CRYSTAL: What is that?

33
00:02:13,741 --> 00:02:14,426
FERRIX: Breath!

34
00:02:15,626 --> 00:02:17,429
PRINCESS CRYSTAL: You
are a clever craftsman.

35
00:02:17,469 --> 00:02:20,378
But you have lied to me, and you will
die, and your scarecrow with you.

36
00:02:23,378 --> 00:02:24,489
What is that?

37
00:02:25,489 --> 00:02:26,277
FERRIX: Tears!

38
00:02:28,877 --> 00:02:31,900
PRINCESS CRYSTAL: Tell me, Myamlak.
What do your brothers do all day?

39
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:37,272
FERRIX: In the morning they pour
clear water over themselves,

40
00:02:37,312 --> 00:02:39,396
and into themselves, for pleasure.

41
00:02:39,436 --> 00:02:43,208
When something grieves them,
salt water runs from their eyes.

42
00:02:43,248 --> 00:02:47,894
When something cheers them, they shake
and hiccup, and their eyes stay dry.

43
00:02:47,934 --> 00:02:51,246
The wet kind we call weeping.
The dry kind, laughter.

44
00:02:52,246 --> 00:02:54,660
PRINCESS CRYSTAL: And where do
you get the energy to slosh about?

45
00:02:56,260 --> 00:02:59,027
FERRIX: Other palefaces walk on four legs.

46
00:02:59,067 --> 00:03:03,038
We perforate them, bake them,
and put them inside ourselves,

47
00:03:03,078 --> 00:03:05,176
through a hole called the mouth.

48
00:03:05,216 --> 00:03:09,160
We call it gastronomy. It has
nothing to do with astronomy.

49
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:12,850
PRINCESS CRYSTAL: So you make yourselves
into coffins for your brothers?

50
00:03:14,450 --> 00:03:18,137
FERRIX: It is not a game,
Highness. Life lives on life.

51
00:03:18,177 --> 00:03:21,158
We have only made the
necessity into an art.

52
00:03:22,558 --> 00:03:26,012
PRINCESS CRYSTAL: It sounds as if it
makes sense, and it does not, not at all.

53
00:03:26,052 --> 00:03:26,903
You are a paleface.

54
00:03:27,703 --> 00:03:29,880
One last test. Give me your hand.

55
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:33,568
Why did you cry out?

56
00:03:34,568 --> 00:03:35,590
FERRIX: From the pain!

57
00:03:39,390 --> 00:03:41,536
Then the Cybercount Cyberhazy landed,

58
00:03:41,576 --> 00:03:44,413
back from the stars, with
a paleface of his own.

59
00:03:45,213 --> 00:03:49,107
CYBERHAZY: Highness, you have been
deceived. Your Myamlak is no paleface.

60
00:03:49,147 --> 00:03:50,279
Here is the real one.

61
00:03:51,679 --> 00:03:53,195
THE PALEFACE: Me paleface!

62
00:03:54,395 --> 00:03:57,684
When it spoke, a pink worm
seemed to crawl in its mouth.

63
00:03:57,724 --> 00:04:00,894
Its breath fogged the mirrors,
and nearby iron rusted.

64
00:04:00,934 --> 00:04:05,096
Now the princess saw what a paleface
was. She was too proud to say so.

65
00:04:05,896 --> 00:04:08,331
PRINCESS CRYSTAL: Let them
fight. The winner has my hand.

66
00:04:09,131 --> 00:04:13,004
FERRIX: If I crush it, the clay will
fall off me, and the steel will show.

67
00:04:13,504 --> 00:04:15,791
POLYPHASE: Then don’t attack. Only defend.

68
00:04:31,991 --> 00:04:35,676
He stood there with no disguise,
waiting for his sentence.

69
00:04:35,716 --> 00:04:38,156
In her crystal face he saw admiration.

70
00:04:39,391 --> 00:04:40,938
Her heart had changed.

71
00:04:45,591 --> 00:04:47,835
They married, and reigned long and well.

72
00:04:47,875 --> 00:04:50,861
The paleface was stuffed
and put in the royal museum,

73
00:04:50,901 --> 00:04:54,784
where it stands to this day, a
scarecrow thinly overgrown with hair.

74
00:04:56,584 --> 00:04:59,392
Some say there never were
any palefaces. Perhaps.

75
00:04:59,432 --> 00:05:01,640
There are fables enough in this world.

76
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:07,095
But even if the story is not true,
there is a grain of sense in it.

